# The app normally FINDS the backend on its own, trying in order:
#   1. this value (explicit override, optional)
#   2. the Metro bundler host on port 5000 (the PC running `expo start`)
#   3. the Metro host on port 5001
#   4. http://10.0.2.2:5000 (Android emulator)
#   5. http://192.168.83.1:5000 (LAN fallback)
# Only set this if the backend runs somewhere else (another machine, a
# non-default port). Find your PC's IP with `ipconfig` (IPv4).
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ vars are inlined when the JS bundle is built — restart
# Expo with `npx expo start -c` after changing this file.
#
# Check it works: open http://<your-ip>:5000/health on the phone's browser.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://192.168.83.1:5000
